# Two-dimensional array and array of arrays.
#
# Derivation (ed.3 6.4.4.4.2 / ed.2 2.4.3.1: an array initialiser lists the
# elements with the rightmost subscript varying most rapidly, so
# m = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]] by rows; a nested initialiser is written per
# sub-array):
#   m[0, *] = 1 2 3 (row sum 6), m[1, *] = 4 5 6 (row sum 15)
#   a[*][0] = 10 40 (col 50), a[*][1] = 20 50 (70), a[*][2] = 30 60 (90)
# cycle 0: i=0 j=0 -> 1, 10, 6, 50
# cycle 1: i=1 j=2 -> 6, 60, 15, 90
# cycle 2: i=0 j=1 -> 2, 20, 6, 70
# cycle 3: i=1 j=0 -> 4, 40, 15, 50
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: i j
outputs: m_ij a_ij rsum csum
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.4.4.4.2 (array initialisation), table 14; ed.2 2.4.3.1
---
0 i=0 j=0 => m_ij=1 a_ij=10 rsum=6 csum=50
1 i=1 j=2 => m_ij=6 a_ij=60 rsum=15 csum=90
2 i=0 j=1 => m_ij=2 a_ij=20 rsum=6 csum=70
3 i=1 j=0 => m_ij=4 a_ij=40 rsum=15 csum=50
